# Catppuccin Mocha theme (accent: mauve)
# Palette: see docs/palette.md. Upstream: https://github.com/catppuccin/palette
#
# tig 2.6.1 has no hex/true-color support, so every colour below is a 256-colour
# stand-in, and there is no Catppuccin port for tig to copy from. Mocha is far
# more saturated than the theme before it, so nearest-RGB no longer dumps half
# the palette onto the greyscale ramp — but it still collides: overlay1 and
# overlay2 both land on color103, subtext0 and subtext1 both on color146, teal
# and sky both on color116. So these stay hand-picked for maximum distinctness
# while keeping each hue recognisable, and docs/palette.md's 256 column is a
# starting point rather than the answer for this file.
#
# They are approximations of approximations; the truecolor tools are the
# reference, not this file.
#
# Only the roles tig actually has are listed — it exposes no string/type/
# function scopes, so most of the syntax palette never reaches it.
#
#   text         #cdd6f4 -> color189   text
#   overlay2     #9399b2 -> color146   (unused; kept for reference)
#   overlay1     #7f849c -> color103   muted chrome, line numbers
#   mauve        #cba6f7 -> color183   THE ACCENT — cursor, titles, dirs, HEAD
#   lavender     #b4befe -> color147   authors, refs, chunk headers
#   pink         #f5c2e7 -> color218   remotes, tracked, prefetch
#   peach        #fab387 -> color216   unstaged changes
#   green        #a6e3a1 -> color151   added / staged / notes
#   red          #f38ba8 -> color211   removed / untracked / replaced
#   yellow       #f9e2af -> color223   changed / tags / stash / commit ids
#   base         #1e1e2e -> color235   text on a filled accent
#   surface0     #313244 -> color237   the one non-default background (blurred
#                                      title and cursor rows)
#
# Backgrounds are left as `default` so tig inherits the terminal's real
# #1e1e2e from Ghostty rather than an approximation — the same reasoning as
# above, applied to the background.

# Layout
set vertical-split = false

# Base UI
color default        color189 default
color cursor          color235 color183
color cursor-blur     color189 color237
color status          color189 default
color title-focus     color235 color183
color title-blur      color189 color237
color search-result   color235 color183
color header          color189 default
color line-number     color103 default
color delimiter       color103 default
color id              color223 default
color date            color189 default
color author          color147 default
color committer       color189 default
color mode            color103 default
color overflow        color103 default
color directory       color183 default
color file            color189 default
color file-size       color103 default

# Diff view
color diff-add        color151  default
color diff-del         color211 default
color diff-header      color183 default
color diff-chunk        color147 default

# Log / commit graph
color graph-commit    color183 default
color main-commit     color189 default
color main-annotated  color147 default
color main-head       color183 default bold
color main-remote     color218 default
color main-tracked    color218 default
color main-tag        color223 default
color main-local-tag  color223 default
color main-ref        color147 default
color main-replace    color211 default
color main-stash      color223 default
color main-note       color151  default
color main-prefetch   color218 default
color main-other      color189 default

# Status view
color stat-none      color103 default
color stat-staged     color151  default
color stat-unstaged    color216 default
color stat-untracked     color211 default

# Help view
color help-group   color183 default bold
color help-action   color189 default

# Tree view
color tree.directory   color183 default
color tree.file        color189 default
